[patterns/itsm-operations/api-microservices/PTN-OPS-API-002-health-check-pattern.md#2-readiness-probe-healthready]

#### 2. Readiness Probe (`/health/ready`)

**Purpose**: Determine if the service can handle traffic (dependencies healthy, initialization complete).

**Validation Criteria** (Comprehensive Checks):
- ✅ **Database connectivity**: Can connect to database and execute simple query
- ✅ **Cache availability**: Redis/Memcached cache responsive
- ✅ **Downstream services**: Critical downstream services reachable
- ✅ **Message queue**: Kafka/RabbitMQ connection healthy
- ✅ **Initialization complete**: Application startup finished (cache loaded, configuration validated)

**Action on Failure**:
- Readiness probe failure → Kubernetes **removes pod from service load balancer**
- Traffic routed only to healthy pods
- Pod NOT restarted—remains running but doesn't receive traffic
- When probe succeeds again → Pod added back to load balancer

**Kubernetes Configuration**:
```yaml
readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health/ready
    port: 8080
    scheme: HTTP
  initialDelaySeconds: 10  # Start checking 10s after startup
  periodSeconds: 5         # Check every 5 seconds (faster than liveness)
  timeoutSeconds: 3        # 3-second timeout
  successThreshold: 1      # 1 success = ready
  failureThreshold: 2      # 2 consecutive failures = not ready → remove from load balancer
```

**Implementation Example** (ASP.NET Core):
```csharp
// Comprehensive readiness check with dependency validation
services.AddHealthChecks()
    // Database health check
    .AddSqlServer(
        connectionString: Configuration.GetConnectionString("ClaimsDB"),
        healthQuery: "SELECT 1",
        name: "claims-database",
        failureStatus: HealthStatus.Unhealthy,  // Database failure = unhealthy
        tags: new[] { "ready", "database" },
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2))

    // Redis cache health check
    .AddRedis(
        redisConnectionString: Configuration.GetConnectionString("Redis"),
        name: "redis-cache",
        failureStatus: HealthStatus.Degraded,  // Cache failure = degraded (not unhealthy)
        tags: new[] { "ready", "cache" },
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2))

    // Downstream service health check
    .AddUrlGroup(
        uri: new Uri("http://eligibility-service:8080/health/ready"),
        name: "eligibility-service",
        failureStatus: HealthStatus.Degraded,
        tags: new[] { "ready", "downstream" },
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2))

    // Custom initialization check
    .AddCheck<InitializationHealthCheck>("initialization",
        failureStatus: HealthStatus.Unhealthy,
        tags: new[] { "ready" });

// Custom health check for initialization status
public class InitializationHealthCheck : IHealthCheck
{
    private readonly IInitializationService _initService;

    public async Task<HealthCheckResult> CheckHealthAsync(HealthCheckContext context)
    {
        if (!_initService.IsInitialized)
        {
            return HealthCheckResult.Unhealthy(
                "Service initialization not complete",
                data: new Dictionary<string, object>
                {
                    { "initializationProgress", _initService.ProgressPercentage },
                    { "estimatedTimeRemaining", _initService.EstimatedTimeRemaining }
                });
        }

        return HealthCheckResult.Healthy(
            "Service fully initialized and ready for traffic");
    }
}

// Configure readiness endpoint
app.UseHealthChecks("/health/ready", new HealthCheckOptions
{
    Predicate = check => check.Tags.Contains("ready"),
    ResponseWriter = UIResponseWriter.WriteHealthCheckUIResponse,  // Detailed JSON
    ResultStatusCodes =
    {
        [HealthStatus.Healthy] = StatusCodes.Status200OK,
        [HealthStatus.Degraded] = StatusCodes.Status200OK,  // Degraded still accepts traffic
        [HealthStatus.Unhealthy] = StatusCodes.Status503ServiceUnavailable
    }
});
```

