### HIPAA Compliance Requirements

**Audit Logging**:

```csharp
// Log all health check results for HIPAA audit trail
public class HealthCheckAuditLogger : IHealthCheckPublisher
{
    private readonly ILogger<HealthCheckAuditLogger> _logger;

    public Task PublishAsync(HealthReport report, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var auditEntry = new
        {
            Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
            Service = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("SERVICE_NAME"),
            OverallStatus = report.Status.ToString(),
            Duration = report.TotalDuration.TotalMilliseconds,
            Checks = report.Entries.Select(e => new
            {
                Name = e.Key,
                Status = e.Value.Status.ToString(),
                Duration = e.Value.Duration.TotalMilliseconds,
                Error = e.Value.Exception?.Message,
                Description = e.Value.Description
            }).ToList(),
            ComplianceClassification = "HIPAA-Audit",
            RetentionYears = 7
        };

        // Log to centralized logging (Splunk/ELK) with HIPAA tag
        _logger.LogInformation(
            "Health check audit: {AuditEntry}",
            JsonSerializer.Serialize(auditEntry));

        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}

// Register audit logger
services.AddHealthChecks()
    .AddCheck<DatabaseHealthCheck>("database")
    .AddCheck<CacheHealthCheck>("cache");

services.Configure<HealthCheckPublisherOptions>(options =>
{
    options.Delay = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    options.Period = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30);
});

services.AddSingleton<IHealthCheckPublisher, HealthCheckAuditLogger>();
```

**HIPAA Audit Requirements Checklist**:

- ✅ **Service Availability Logging**: All health check results logged with timestamp for 7-year retention
- ✅ **Dependency Health Tracking**: Database, cache, downstream service health logged for audit trail
- ✅ **Failure Root Cause**: Health check failures logged with detailed error messages
- ✅ **Access to PHI Systems**: Health checks validate connectivity to PHI data stores (database, cache)
- ✅ **Incident Response**: Health check failures trigger alerts enabling <15 minute response time
- ✅ **Change Management**: Health check configuration changes tracked in Git, peer reviewed

